# S0c: the REFERENCE for A1 and the arms: the same eight-seat 262k attach and exactness smoke (the 8x262k-gate tests, concurrent8_steady included) on the CONTROL gate profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-gate (no levers, no quad blocks, the
# pool that profile states), so that the later arms have a run in this pack to compare their answer hashes, accepted tokens and verify-round counts with. READ: admission passed at capacity 262144,
# every answer completes, c2_smoke_check clean, no stall. RECORD per request the answer hash, the accepted tokens and the verify rounds (concurrent8_code_equal, concurrent8_code, concurrent8_steady). Duration (estimate): 90 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/u1 development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/u1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-u1-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/u1 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-u1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_steady,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
